# Prismattyc child-facing truecolor terminfo.
#
# Default child TERM is `prismattyc-kitty` so producers that key on TERM
# containing "kitty" (Claude Code v2.1.238: `TERM.includes("kitty")` before
# TERM_PROGRAM) emit Kitty graphics APC and CSI-u. `prismattyc-direct` is a
# name alias.
#
# Base caps come from xterm-direct (planner: do not blend a 256-color setaf
# with colors#0x1000000). Do NOT `use=xterm-kitty`: that entry is 256-color
# and advertises sequences Prism does not implement (styled underline Su/
# Smulx/Setulc, strikethrough smxx, Sync, OSC 52 Ms, DECSCUSR Ss/Se).
# Advertising those is the failure mode.
#
# Extra user capabilities are only Kitty-shaped bits Prism actually handles:
#   fullkbd     — CSI-u keyboard (keyboard encoding / F19)
#   Tc          — 24-bit color boolean (F10); COLORTERM=truecolor still set
#   setrgbf/b   — ISO-colon RGB (F10)
#   BE/BD/PS/PE — bracketed paste DECSET 2004 (F11)
#   XF, fe/fd   — focus in/out DECSET 1004 (F17)
#
# Kitty graphics itself is APC `_G`, not a terminfo cap. The name is the
# graphics signal; the caps above are the rest of the honest Kitty subset.
#
# Compile (from repo root):
#   tic -x -o terminfo terminfo/prism-direct.src
#
prismattyc-kitty|prismattyc-direct|Prismattyc terminal with 24-bit color and Kitty protocol,
	use=xterm-direct,
	fullkbd,
	Tc,
	XF,
	BE=\E[?2004h,
	BD=\E[?2004l,
	PS=\E[200~,
	PE=\E[201~,
	fe=\E[?1004h,
	fd=\E[?1004l,
	setrgbf=\E[38:2:%p1%d:%p2%d:%p3%dm,
	setrgbb=\E[48:2:%p1%d:%p2%d:%p3%dm,
